Okay, in my current game on NAO, I'm in the
late middle game:  I've found and marked the
vibrating square, placed the candelabrum and
the bell on burned Elbereths on that level, and
now, before I go wake up mister Wizard, I'm
working on whatever other preparations I want
to complete before the final push to victory.

One of these preparations is digging paths
through the mazes in Gehennom.  I'm lawful,
so I fully expect Mr. mysterious force to drop
me in random places in these mazes on a
number of occasions before I get the amulet
back up to the main dungeon.  Meanwhile,
Rodney will probably be summoning nasties
to surround me and interrupt my progress.
I have controlled teleport, of course, but my
max power is not terribly impressive, so there
may be times when I need to conserve,
especially since I've chosen to make this
Valkyrie something of a spellcaster.  Potions
of gain energy haven't been particularly in
abundance this game, so unless somebody
knows a nice easy recipe for those...  there
are going to be times when I need to walk.

So I'm trying to make some nice easy paths
through the mazes.

My question is, how much is clearly enough?
Bear in mind, I'm a beginning player and have
never carried a game all the way through to
ascension (indeed, this is only the third time
I've got the castle wand -- first time on a
public server), so I'm not going for a speed
ascension here or anything, and I don't want
to leave myself in a bind, even a minor one,
if it can be avoided by preparing a bit more.

I've heard tell of people digging away *all* the
walls in Gehennom, so that every level is a
pure wide open field, but I'm pretty sure that's
excessive.

Is it enough to have a grid of roads every 5-7
tiles, vertically and horizontally?  Here's the
kind of thing I'm talking about...

 
