Is there anything to be gained by digging more (other
than pushing up the turn count and giving the game
time to generate more mundane monsters), or is that
plenty?  The main thoroughfares between the stairs
are several tiles wide, but should I make some of
the others -- perhaps a couple each of the vertical
and horizontal ones -- two tiles wide, instead of one?
Or is that pointless?

Should I cast the light spell everywhere on the level, in
case I get plopped down there, or is it enough to light the
areas around the stairs and such, as in the screenshot?

On the one hand, I'm starting to think I might be
overpreparing a little.  On the other hand, this is the
first time I've got past the castle on a public server,
so I do *not* want to take unnecessary changes and
end up failing to ascend because of something I just
didn't bother to do.

Will further digging improve my chances?
How much more digging?

(Running out of food is not a problem at this point,
as I have a ring of slow digestion and monsters are
still spawning regularly.  I'm hardly even eating any
of the corpses any more, now that I have a good
collection of intrinsics.  I suppose I do need to get
enlightened at some point and check to see if there's
one I missed; oddly, I don't think I've seen a wand
of enlightenment in this game, but I imagine I can
find another way, especially since I really only
need to check once.  Or I could polypile some of
those spare wands of sleep and speed monster
and slow monster and whatnot.)


